bas-cpp (1.0.2) testing; urgency=medium

  * Security and access-control demo:
    - Add tanks_game: ncurses dual-device tank demo with per-realm login,
      ACL policy panel, one-shot elevation, and batch mode for scripts.
    - Split tanks_rbac (SecurityManager wiring, permission checks, batch CLI)
      from tanks_game UI; built-in TankA/TankB user and policy stores
      (no external JSON fixtures).
    - Add RealmPolicyStore for per-realm ACL routing with global fallback.
    - Remove LoginPolicy; mark login identities with IdentitySource::Login
      and clear them on realm logout / session switch.
    - Add SecurityManager::authenticate() and checkSubjectPermission()
      for credential checks without changing the active session.
  * Volume backend fixes:
    - MemDevice: rename OwnType::NONE to VIEW (read-only buffer) and add
      BORROWED for writable non-owning buffers.
    - exFAT: parse boot sector via explicit little-endian byte fields.
    - ext4: use shared directory node refs; fix cache invalidation,
      getBaseName, and file/directory creation write ordering.
    - FAT32: improve rename/remove bookkeeping; Fat32_test mounts images
      via BlockDevice instead of read-only MemDevice views.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Fri, 05 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0800

bas-cpp (1.0.1) testing; urgency=medium

  * Refactor volume backends into dedicated modules:
    - src/volume/zip (MemoryZip)
    - src/volume/fat32 (Fat32Volume + file streams)
    - src/volume/ext4 (Ext4Volume + file streams)
  * Add FAT32 image volume support and wire it through VolumeManager.
  * Add ext2/ext3/ext4 image volume support with optional libext2fs linking.
  * Avoid full-image buffering for FAT32/EXT file access by introducing
    dedicated RandomInputStream/OutputStream implementations.
  * Switch Ext4Volume to on-demand path->inode resolution and cache
    directory indexes by inode to avoid expensive full-tree mount scans.
  * Add Ext4Volume execution context primitives (uid/gid/groups + IUserDb)
    and enforce mode-based access checks for traversal/read/list paths.
  * Add image-based tests for FAT32 and EXT volume backends.
  * Update build wiring and includes for relocated MemoryZip paths.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Tue, 24 Mar 2026 18:30:00 +0800

